  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the value of $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{\u230a1-x\u230b}}{x}$ at $x=-1.5.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\u230ax\u230b$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n\u230ax\u230b=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.5) & =\\frac{{e}^{\u230a1-(-1.5)\u230b}}{(-1.5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{\u230a1+1.5\u230b}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{\u230a2.5\u230b}}{1.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u230a2.5\u230b=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.5) & =-\\frac{{e}^{\u230a2.5\u230b}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{1.5} \\\\  & =-4.926\\,03\u2026 \\\\  & \u2248-4.93,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
